Figure 1 demonstrates the comparative adjuvanticity of Nano-11 and aluminum hydroxide (AH) when combined with recombinant protective antigen (rPA) in immunized mice. Both adjuvants significantly increased rPA-specific IgG titers compared to rPA alone. Nano-11 exhibited comparable immunopotentiation to AH at higher dosages (200 and 50 µg). Importantly, at a lower dose of 12.5 µg, Nano-11 induced significantly higher antibody titers than AH, suggesting its superior efficacy in enhancing immune responses at reduced concentrations.